  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection response for the internal displacement situation in the North-West/South-West regions and Shelter/NFI response in the Far North</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection, shelter and essential household item assistance to internally displaced persons, returnees and host community members in the North-West and Far North regions of Cameroon. This UNHCR project establishes protection monitoring mechanisms, provides unconditional cash assistance, distributes essential household item kits, supports community empowerment and quick impact initiatives, and helps internally displaced persons access civil documentation. The protection component of the project provides humanitarian assistance to 30,000 people, including 9,000 women, 9,000 men, 12,000 children, and including 1,000 persons with disabilities. The shelter and essential household item component of the project provides humanitarian assistance to 20,650 people, including 3,400 women, 2,350 men, 14,900 children, and including 1,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
